  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S2 was ultimately rewritten so that exceeding 5% triggers regulator review and corrective action, with sales suspended only at regulator discretion, removing the automatic stop-sale that would have hit Hearth 10; per-model results go to purchasers but not the public. S5 keeps the 8-per-100,000 mandatory recall trigger with no transition, which bears directly on Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9). S3's 24-month new-unit deadline lies outside the stated acceptable range, and its 6-year retrofit window favours Northwind's 38% shut-off coverage."
